[$in title:["Casts"]]
[$in description:["Explicit cast syntax, target contexts, fallible conversion and cast evidence in Moth."]]
[$in head:[language_theme_head]]

[navbar]
[sidebar]
listed = sync_navigation(sidebar_id)!
[section, $md:
    # Casts

    With `cast`, the value supplies the source type and the place that
    receives it supplies the target. For example, returning a cast from a
    function with a `U16` result asks for a `U16`. When the conversion can
    fail, use `catch` to handle it locally or let the enclosing function's
    error contract deliver it. See @../progress (Progress) for compiler
    and backend support.
]

